---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lead={`The rules for using ${site.name}. By using the site, you agree to these terms.`}
  description={`Terms of use for ${site.name}, the free interactive science lab.`}
  updated={site.legalUpdated}
>
  <p>
    {site.name} (<a href={site.url}>{site.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>) is a free educational website created and run
    by {site.creator.name}, {site.venue}. In these terms, “we” and “us” mean {site.name} and its creator.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Using the site</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} provides free interactive science simulations and educational content. You may use the site for personal
    learning, studying and teaching. You agree not to misuse the site, for example by attempting to disrupt it, gain
    unauthorized access to it, or scrape it in a way that places an unreasonable load on it.
    The site is intended for high school and college students, teachers and other learners; if you are under 13, please
    use it with a parent, guardian or teacher.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Educational purpose only</h2>
  <p>
    All content is provided for general educational purposes. Simulations are simplified models that do not represent
    every detail of real systems. Content about anatomy, physiology, health or medicine is not medical advice. Please
    read our full <a href="/disclaimer/">educational and medical disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Classroom and personal use</h2>
  <p>
    Teachers and students are welcome to display simulations in class, link to pages, and share them with learners. You
    may not copy, republish or sell the site’s text, simulations, code or graphics as your own, or present them on
    another website, without our written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The text, simulations, illustrations, design and code on {site.name} are original works created for {site.name}, or
    open-source software and fonts used under their licences, and are protected by copyright and other laws. Names of third-party products and organizations are used
    for identification only.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to make our content accurate and to cite reputable sources, but we cannot guarantee that every page is
    complete, current or free of errors. If you find a mistake, please <a href="/contact/">let us know</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. External links</h2>
  <p>
    Pages may link to other websites, such as textbooks and references. We do not control and are not responsible for
    the content or practices of those sites.
  </p>

  <h2>7. No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, express or implied. We do not
    guarantee that the site will always be available, uninterrupted or compatible with every device.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.name} is not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of, or
    inability to use, the site or its content, including any decision made based on it.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is free to use and may display advertising, such as Google AdSense, to cover its running costs. Ads are
    provided by third parties; we do not endorse the products advertised and are not responsible for advertisers’ sites.
    Please do not click ads on purpose to support the site — only click an ad if you are genuinely interested in it. How
    advertising uses cookies is explained in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of {site.jurisdiction}. Any dispute arising from them or from your use of the site
    shall be brought before the proper courts of {site.venue}, without prejudice to any rights you have under the
    consumer laws of the country where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. Changes take effect when they are posted on this page, and the “last
    updated” date above will change. Continuing to use the site means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms? Send them through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> (choose “Privacy or legal
    question”).
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
